# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build artifacts — the installer ships via Releases (CI-built), never committed to the repo
*.exe

# The dreams stay on disk (keeper's call, 2026-07-15). They were pooled here 07-13→07-14 so every
# bed could read every dream as the one dreamer's own — a good idea aimed at the wrong repo. This
# one is public, the sync was unattended, and a dream recombines whatever the day held: it turned
# out to include the keeper's city, his spending, and his life. No unattended process of ours
# publishes. The FRAMEWORK ships so anyone can grow their own dreams; the dreams themselves don't.
dreams/

# Harvest indexes point INTO transcripts, and a transcript holds whatever the day held. The
# index is pointers only and still doesn't ship: a pointer to the keeper's life is a pointer
# to the keeper's life. Same call as dreams/, one layer of indirection out.
harvest/

# Generated by the PreCompact checkpoint. State of a moment, not a record.
exo_memory/loop/CHECKPOINT.md

# The listening ledger. Kept out of the repo for CHURN, not for privacy — the keeper ruled on that
# directly (2026-07-29): "I do not care who sees what I listen to". It is an append-only log that
# grows every second something plays and is of no use to a reader. The Adagio fixture under
# src-tauri/tests/ is the artifact worth keeping, and it IS committed. Note the distinction from
# dreams/ above, which stays out for the original reason: a dream recombines whatever the day held.
consonance/**/heard.jsonl
heard.jsonl
consonance/**/field.json
field.json

# Recorded analysis frames and the flag that arms them. A frame list is what the keeper was
# listening to at 12 readings a second — same call as dreams/ and heard.jsonl. The RECORD flag is
# machine state, not a record.
consonance/**/frames.jsonl
frames.jsonl
consonance/**/RECORD
